235
00:18:05,663 --> 00:18:08,926
[SPEAKER_01]: Why did I choose... what did I choose to do with my life that led me to this point?

236
00:18:09,526 --> 00:18:18,093
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you say, why did I... why did I choose to go and live on top of a mountain now, when I could have gone to... well, because at first I've chosen to become a monk, ten, eleven years ago.

237
00:18:18,654 --> 00:18:20,115
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, I've chosen to come to Sri Lanka.

238
00:18:20,535 --> 00:18:22,617
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, I've chosen to find a more secluded place.

239
00:18:22,697 --> 00:18:26,440
[SPEAKER_01]: And now, I have this particular choice that results out of that.

240
00:18:27,801 --> 00:18:29,722
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in that sense, no matter how

241
00:18:30,857 --> 00:18:32,018
[SPEAKER_01]: Spontaneous, the choice is.

242
00:18:32,658 --> 00:18:38,881
[SPEAKER_01]: You are responsible for it, because of the previous choices you made, because of the previous choices you made, because of the previous choices you made.

243
00:18:39,121 --> 00:18:45,345
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all of the choices you made, the options, so to speak, were given to you before and initially.

244
00:18:46,545 --> 00:18:50,067
[SPEAKER_01]: You do choose a direction, and within that direction, you choose other directions, another direction.

245
00:18:50,387 --> 00:18:54,950
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes, circumstance, accident, things happen, but that's all part of the human realm.

246
00:18:55,660 --> 00:19:05,272
[SPEAKER_01]: And that just shows you that no matter how volitional your choices are, they're always going to remain, well, out of your control.

247
00:19:05,873 --> 00:19:11,840
[SPEAKER_01]: Because no matter what you chose, what you built, what direction you took, it can all be taken away in one stroke of bad luck.

248
00:19:12,819 --> 00:19:15,481
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not like it's in someone else's control.

249
00:19:15,762 --> 00:19:15,942
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

250
00:19:16,082 --> 00:19:17,783
[SPEAKER_00]: Or something else's control.

251
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:25,290
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's when you project your sense of self that you can't let go of externally, and then you end up assuming a god, a god, and then you pray, and then you become super.

252
00:19:25,430 --> 00:19:26,091
[SPEAKER_01]: Or a devil.

253
00:19:26,171 --> 00:19:28,353
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rather, then you tap into the kind of

254
00:19:29,079 --> 00:19:35,785
[SPEAKER_01]: Naturally inclined superstitiousness of people, which is basically praying to something external, because you recognize that.

255
00:19:35,805 --> 00:19:45,094
[SPEAKER_01]: You recognize that no matter how much effort you put, how far you go, how careful you choose, everything can be taken away the next second from you and destroyed.

256
00:19:45,515 --> 00:19:52,681
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what you do, because you don't know that you're supposed to let go of your own sense of self, you don't see that as the way out, you can't even conceive.

