00:19:53,362 --> 00:19:54,543
[SPEAKER_01]: Yourself not being yours.

258
00:19:56,004 --> 00:19:58,286
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, you just end up projecting that sense of self externally.

259
00:19:58,346 --> 00:20:05,232
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you end up worshipping trees, aes, stones, deities, whatever, externally, through that sense of self, as if...

260
00:20:05,732 --> 00:20:06,092
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

261
00:20:06,112 --> 00:20:13,498
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize this is not in my control, but you, by default, assume that it's in someone else's control, or something else's control, which is still taking a self.

262
00:20:13,639 --> 00:20:14,299
[SPEAKER_01]: Making assumptions.

263
00:20:14,319 --> 00:20:14,499
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

264
00:20:14,519 --> 00:20:15,600
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you become superstitious.

265
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:18,062
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't believe in anything, you become, like, magical.

266
00:20:18,603 --> 00:20:21,425
[SPEAKER_01]: You think, oh, if I step on my left foot first, it's going to be a bad luck.

267
00:20:21,445 --> 00:20:21,565
[SPEAKER_01]: Just

268
00:20:22,826 --> 00:20:25,007
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's still projected in the same external principle.

269
00:20:26,507 --> 00:20:35,370
[SPEAKER_00]: But, eh... if I look back to why... if I really ask myself, why am I choosing this?

270
00:20:35,410 --> 00:20:35,670
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

271
00:20:36,330 --> 00:20:43,052
[SPEAKER_00]: And I look back in general, as I said the other day, it was like, well, you would choose... you choose what is pleasant.

272
00:20:43,738 --> 00:20:45,980
[SPEAKER_00]: You choose what you think is pleasant.

273
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:49,863
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it'll come down, like, right to the to the core, basically.

274
00:20:49,883 --> 00:20:51,284
[SPEAKER_01]: You choose based on how you feel.

275
00:20:51,464 --> 00:20:55,828
[SPEAKER_00]: Like you say, most often, you're, uh, you're craving for pleasure.

276
00:20:56,969 --> 00:21:05,676
[SPEAKER_00]: The delight in pleasure is the reason, well, for doing many of the things you do.

277
00:21:05,716 --> 00:21:06,817
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not the reason for choice.

278
00:21:07,732 --> 00:21:11,495
[SPEAKER_01]: Because choice is one of the aggregates.

279
00:21:12,076 --> 00:21:13,076
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not the reason.

280
00:21:13,437 --> 00:21:14,958
[SPEAKER_01]: It's origin.

281
00:21:15,338 --> 00:21:17,940
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just the reason why you choose certain choices.

282
00:21:18,181 --> 00:21:20,602
[SPEAKER_01]: But the nature of choice remains regardless of the craving.

283
00:21:21,243 --> 00:21:22,424
[SPEAKER_01]: Choice is one of the aggregates.

284
00:21:24,165 --> 00:21:26,167
[SPEAKER_01]: The intentions, cetanā, that's already choice.

285
00:21:26,207 --> 00:21:27,188
[SPEAKER_01]: So, everything is intentional.

286
00:21:27,268 --> 00:21:28,709
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything is directional in that sense.

287
00:21:29,630 --> 00:21:32,072
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's just what intention you attend.

288
00:21:34,825 --> 00:21:38,267
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then your choice becomes down to attending to things.

289
00:21:39,087 --> 00:21:43,309
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why the Buddha would often say, he carefully attends, not careless.

290
00:21:43,369 --> 00:21:48,051
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you carelessly attend, then you already start fueling a certain directions.

291
00:21:48,511 --> 00:21:57,215
[SPEAKER_01]: So, by the time the choices are kind of crystallized as options, you're actually fully responsible, because you've been dwelling on those things in your mind.

292
00:21:57,955 --> 00:22:04,278
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if while somebody carelessly attends to the sign of beauty and ends up lusting after it,

293
00:22:06,383 --> 00:22:15,008
[SPEAKER_01]: He can't be surprised that then his choice is about pursuing the central pleasure, or, okay, saying no to it, but there's nothing in between.

294
00:22:15,029 --> 00:22:19,491
[SPEAKER_01]: He can't say anything in between, because it's all about sensuality, because his mind's been burning.

295
00:22:19,531 --> 00:22:21,092
[SPEAKER_01]: And obviously, then he'll choose to pursue it.

296
00:22:21,573 --> 00:22:22,854
[SPEAKER_01]: He's not strong enough to say no.

297
00:22:23,934 --> 00:22:25,916
[SPEAKER_01]: The choice of no is present in everything.

298
00:22:26,636 --> 00:22:29,758
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's when you realize that you can, you yourself, can undermine everything as well.

