00:22:30,158 --> 00:22:31,879
[SPEAKER_00]: But this thing, there's

300
00:22:33,675 --> 00:22:35,375
[SPEAKER_00]: That knowledge has to be presented to you.

301
00:22:35,875 --> 00:22:38,216
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to know beforehand, yeah, in order to learn.

302
00:22:38,296 --> 00:22:39,156
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, there's a different way.

303
00:22:39,196 --> 00:22:41,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah, I didn't know there was a choice there.

304
00:22:41,476 --> 00:22:41,636
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh.

305
00:22:41,996 --> 00:22:48,218
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your intentions, your intentions become fueled by the simple attention.

306
00:22:48,698 --> 00:22:50,038
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, what you attend more.

307
00:22:50,698 --> 00:22:53,058
[SPEAKER_01]: What you attend at expense of what.

308
00:22:55,439 --> 00:23:02,260
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, those intentions then, determined further down the line, cause the forms of choices you made in your life.

309
00:23:03,818 --> 00:23:30,305
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you were to know that, if you just then, no matter what choices you made, if you still... like the example I gave, the man who wants to leave it all behind, but feels responsible for his family and he can't give it in, if he still doesn't give in to bad faith, and if he still doesn't obscure the sense of guilt that he himself brought himself into that position, if he starts to attend constantly on the freedom from suffering, on the Buddha's teaching or whatever, sooner or later,

310
00:23:31,340 --> 00:23:35,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Eventually, maybe not soon, but eventually, he will build enough resolve to leave it all behind.

311
00:23:36,763 --> 00:23:40,265
[SPEAKER_01]: It just might take longer than somebody who doesn't have a family and kids and everything else.

312
00:23:41,425 --> 00:23:43,086
[SPEAKER_01]: But they don't attempt it.

313
00:23:43,727 --> 00:23:43,887
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

314
00:23:43,927 --> 00:23:44,987
[SPEAKER_01]: They just look at it.

315
00:23:45,067 --> 00:23:47,829
[SPEAKER_01]: I want to do it right now, but I can't do it because of my family.

316
00:23:48,549 --> 00:23:52,952
[SPEAKER_01]: And then they disown responsibility for it as if it wasn't them who built that family.

317
00:23:54,232 --> 00:23:55,653
[SPEAKER_01]: And then they don't think about it anymore.

318
00:23:56,491 --> 00:24:02,154
[SPEAKER_01]: And then they just cement, cement it, like, cement over it, as if it's done, it's sorted.

319
00:24:02,454 --> 00:24:07,037
[SPEAKER_01]: I cannot possibly do it because of this, and I'm not responsible for it anyway.

320
00:24:07,057 --> 00:24:10,119
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, I'll just have to do what I can, with what I got.

321
00:24:10,399 --> 00:24:25,768
[SPEAKER_00]: You'll see that the choice to leave the world behind, or freedom, the choice to be free from suffering, the guy who's just living his life, whatever, having a family, whatever, you know, that choice,

322
00:24:28,766 --> 00:24:38,172
[SPEAKER_01]: No, but what I'm talking about is, like, why would you... why would he choose that, or why he wouldn't choose that?

323
00:24:38,233 --> 00:24:40,854
[SPEAKER_01]: Why he wouldn't be able to choose, which is what you asked originally.

324
00:24:41,575 --> 00:24:51,902
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because he's either too weak in regard to it, to such choice, too weak to say the... too weak to stir himself up, too weak to accept the pain that would come with it initially,

325
00:24:52,820 --> 00:24:57,923
[SPEAKER_01]: Too weak to see through the immediate pleasure that appears as not fully gratifying.

326
00:24:57,943 --> 00:25:02,845
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, you know, it's pleasant to be in the safety of your home and family, but in the long run, it's more dangerous.

327
00:25:03,506 --> 00:25:07,568
[SPEAKER_01]: But he's too weak to see any of that, because he's not attending to it on a daily basis.

328
00:25:08,837 --> 00:25:21,428
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, if he was to not give in to that kind of cover-up of his own guilt for his own choices, cover-up of his own responsibility for his own choices, he would be able to keep dwelling on it, to attend to it.

329
00:25:22,288 --> 00:25:32,357
[SPEAKER_01]: And if he does attend sufficiently, there won't be no amount of children or family to keep you in their life, if you recognize the true danger of human existence, the peril of it.

