559
00:42:28,924 --> 00:42:33,885
[SPEAKER_01]: So you can't just think about feeling without involving perception and intention.

560
00:42:40,667 --> 00:42:41,648
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can discern them.

561
00:42:42,748 --> 00:42:55,772
[SPEAKER_01]: As they arise simultaneously as this kind of group, like welded trio, you can still, within that, discern them, discern these separate elements.

562
00:42:56,859 --> 00:43:00,723
[SPEAKER_01]: And thus, intentions intend, feelings fuel.

563
00:43:01,143 --> 00:43:03,925
[SPEAKER_01]: Why does intention intend this, or intention intend that?

564
00:43:04,406 --> 00:43:14,415
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, once you stop acting out of your feeling, once you fully understood the feelings, you wouldn't be intending based on how you feel, because that was inconceivable to begin with.

565
00:43:14,455 --> 00:43:16,177
[SPEAKER_01]: Intentions cannot mix with feelings.

566
00:43:16,957 --> 00:43:18,779
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a different domain, different aggregate.

567
00:43:21,298 --> 00:43:22,679
[SPEAKER_01]: They're completely oblivious to each other.

568
00:43:22,699 --> 00:43:24,401
[SPEAKER_01]: Intentions are intentions.

569
00:43:24,782 --> 00:43:25,803
[SPEAKER_01]: They intend.

570
00:43:25,843 --> 00:43:26,503
[SPEAKER_01]: Feelings are feelings.

571
00:43:26,523 --> 00:43:26,944
[SPEAKER_01]: They feel.

572
00:43:27,204 --> 00:43:30,027
