877
01:04:05,376 --> 01:04:05,616
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

878
01:04:05,676 --> 01:04:06,657
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe in the future.

879
01:04:06,697 --> 01:04:08,397
[SPEAKER_01]: So you chose to not be ready.

880
01:04:09,158 --> 01:04:11,059
[SPEAKER_01]: You chose that to be the case.

881
01:04:11,899 --> 01:04:13,060
[SPEAKER_01]: And sometimes, you know, things...

882
01:04:13,892 --> 01:04:15,653
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, it depends on what you attend.

883
01:04:15,993 --> 01:04:18,595
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, things can get very subtle.

884
01:04:19,095 --> 01:04:24,838
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not necessarily bad, or rather, it's not necessarily unwholesome, but it can be unwholesome.

885
01:04:25,619 --> 01:04:26,579
[SPEAKER_01]: So, say you are hungry.

886
01:04:28,020 --> 01:04:30,702
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need the food in order to not die.

887
01:04:31,942 --> 01:04:36,345
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, at the same time, you choose only the food that you like.

888
01:04:38,530 --> 01:04:44,872
[SPEAKER_01]: So you're clearly, basically, acting out of lust for taste.

889
01:04:45,732 --> 01:04:48,513
[SPEAKER_01]: That kind of also implies eating the food.

890
01:04:49,373 --> 01:04:51,773
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's why you should, like, attend carefully.

891
01:04:52,954 --> 01:04:56,034
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, the contemplation that we chant in the morning back in the monastery.

892
01:04:56,955 --> 01:04:58,215
