893
01:04:59,495 --> 01:05:06,017
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, okay, there's no question, you abstain from sex, you abstain from killing, you abstain from lying, but you can't abstain from eating, because you'll die.

894
01:05:07,095 --> 01:05:08,056
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have to eat.

895
01:05:08,476 --> 01:05:12,278
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you can say, well, I will eat only things I don't like.

896
01:05:12,378 --> 01:05:16,000
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's not... that's again putting on an external decision.

897
01:05:17,280 --> 01:05:23,903
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you do only what you don't like, then you might start liking torturing yourself.

898
01:05:25,664 --> 01:05:28,566
[SPEAKER_01]: You might start enjoying that unwholesomely.

899
01:05:28,586 --> 01:05:30,007
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence, there won't be any wisdom arising.

900
01:05:30,647 --> 01:05:30,767
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

901
01:05:30,787 --> 01:05:36,790
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you just want to make sure that while you're eating, you make sure that you're active eating,

902
01:05:38,662 --> 01:05:41,883
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't get rooted in unwholesome desire for the pleasant taste.

903
01:05:42,624 --> 01:05:47,286
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, you won't be running away from nice food that you like, that you liked.

904
01:05:47,966 --> 01:05:49,307
[SPEAKER_01]: But you won't be affected by it.

905
01:05:49,667 --> 01:05:50,247
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the thing.

906
01:05:50,587 --> 01:05:59,891
[SPEAKER_01]: Because people think, oh, I really want to eat dish A on account of dish B, which I don't really like, so I should really go with what I don't like.

907
01:06:00,812 --> 01:06:02,853
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's just like projecting it externally.

908
01:06:03,840 --> 01:06:07,103
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, putting responsibility on that which you don't like.

909
01:06:07,723 --> 01:06:09,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Saying, I will choose what I don't like.

910
01:06:09,325 --> 01:06:16,231
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure, you can do it once or twice, but sooner or later, you will get dependent on the view to always do the opposite of what you want to do.

911
01:06:16,251 --> 01:06:17,352
[SPEAKER_01]: i.e.

912
01:06:17,432 --> 01:06:24,738
[SPEAKER_01]: you will become dependent on the view to torture yourself, to cause, to intentionally inflict pain to yourself.

913
01:06:24,998 --> 01:06:26,399
[SPEAKER_01]: Sooner or later, you can't sustain it.

914
01:06:27,620 --> 01:06:30,283
[SPEAKER_01]: But what you want to do, basically, is recognize, I have to eat.

915
01:06:31,048 --> 01:06:33,469
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whether I eat dish A or B, doesn't matter.

916
01:06:34,230 --> 01:06:54,060
[SPEAKER_01]: I prefer dish A to dish B. I might eat both, and then remain mindful in terms of the dish B, to not be hating and thinking about dish A, while I'm eating dish B, and at the same time, while I'm eating dish A, to not be like, well, overjoyed on account of it, or careless in regard to the experience of taste of the dish A.

917
01:06:54,880 --> 01:06:57,882
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you remain mindful in regard to both tastes, because you have to eat.

918
01:06:59,609 --> 01:07:05,571
[SPEAKER_01]: And, above all, you remain mindful as to why you have to eat, in order to sustain the body.

919
01:07:06,411 --> 01:07:18,114
[SPEAKER_01]: If that thought, literally, if that thought remains established in you, you will not overdo the joy when it comes to the dish you like, nor will you be too concerned when it comes to the dish you don't like.

920
01:07:18,574 --> 01:07:18,794
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

921
01:07:18,814 --> 01:07:20,755
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the point is to eat whatever.

922
01:07:22,129 --> 01:07:28,791
[SPEAKER_01]: And you remain rooted in that, through your mindfulness, means there won't be any prize given to the unwholesome.

923
01:07:30,392 --> 01:07:41,916
[SPEAKER_01]: You carelessly attend to what you're eating, you forget why you're eating, or rather you forget to root things in the right reasons for eating, you will inevitably be taken by what?

924
01:07:42,876 --> 01:07:43,536
[SPEAKER_01]: By the senses.

925
01:07:43,596 --> 01:07:47,037
[SPEAKER_01]: You will be taken by that which is the strongest, which is the pool of the taste.

926
01:07:49,987 --> 01:07:53,870
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why the same act of eating can be rūcā and kundalini, and you're responsible for that.

927
01:07:54,630 --> 01:07:59,614
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't have to... and when you start looting yourself properly and establish from there, then you wouldn't care.

928
01:07:59,674 --> 01:08:04,898
[SPEAKER_01]: As the Buddha said, like I have disciples who live only on one handful of rice every second day.

929
01:08:05,459 --> 01:08:14,866
[SPEAKER_01]: While at that time, I would be eating like the finest curries, and I would sometimes eat a bowl full to the brim.

930
01:08:15,848 --> 01:08:25,675
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he would eat two alms bowls to the brim of the nicest food, while he has disciples who live on a handful of rice.

931
01:08:27,537 --> 01:08:33,941
[SPEAKER_01]: If that was the goal of practice, to live on... they would not be respecting him any... in any way whatsoever.

932
01:08:34,262 --> 01:08:41,527
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not... the goal of the practice is to not be affected by the food, to not be affected by the senses, to not be turned...

933
01:08:43,780 --> 01:08:49,186
[SPEAKER_01]: To not being made rooted in unwholesome based on the pull of the senses, that's the goal of the practice.

934
01:08:49,767 --> 01:08:56,254
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whether it's a pleasant taste, touch, sounds, so on, it will not pull you into unwholesome.

935
01:08:56,434 --> 01:08:57,516
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the goal of the practice.

936
01:08:58,357 --> 01:09:00,539
[SPEAKER_01]: When you establish that, then you can eat whatever.

937
01:09:02,560 --> 01:09:04,442
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you establish the principle and then you're not pulled.

938
01:09:04,802 --> 01:09:15,934
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, yeah, the Buddha can have the finest silk robes and three bowls of food in front of him, if he wants, and you'll still respect him as much as you did on the first day, when he was just living as an ascetic.

939
01:09:16,615 --> 01:09:19,318
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, when he's kind of frequented by the kings and everything, you'll respect him.

940
01:09:19,498 --> 01:09:20,098
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense.

941
01:09:20,159 --> 01:09:20,359
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

942
01:09:20,379 --> 01:09:22,520
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you know where the goal is, and you understood what he's teaching was.

943
01:09:22,840 --> 01:09:24,321
[SPEAKER_01]: And that teaching frees you from suffering.

944
01:09:24,762 --> 01:09:29,745
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you might choose to live under a root of tree, enjoying one handful of rice every three days, because you don't need more.

945
01:09:30,085 --> 01:09:33,688
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what makes you happy and content, and not disturbed and peaceful.

946
01:09:34,448 --> 01:09:36,930
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, you'll still respect him while he lives in a palace.

947
01:09:37,751 --> 01:09:39,532
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that was never the point of the practice.

948
01:09:39,552 --> 01:09:40,232
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, the external.

949
01:09:41,193 --> 01:09:42,074
[SPEAKER_00]: It's good.

950
01:09:42,154 --> 01:09:44,896
[SPEAKER_00]: Epictetus says it's very similar.

951
01:09:44,916 --> 01:09:46,136
[SPEAKER_00]: The thing about food.

952
01:09:46,637 --> 01:09:46,837
[SPEAKER_01]: Uh-huh.

953
01:09:46,997 --> 01:09:48,138
[SPEAKER_00]: Being at a banquet and then...

954
01:09:48,750 --> 01:09:50,271
[SPEAKER_00]: Food comes your way.

955
01:09:51,331 --> 01:09:53,092
[SPEAKER_00]: You just take, you know, what you need.

956
01:09:53,752 --> 01:09:56,433
[SPEAKER_00]: But you don't like to call, grab, eat more than you need.

957
01:09:56,753 --> 01:10:03,795
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, if you happen to come across that luxurious food comes, happens to be... You have it.

958
01:10:04,216 --> 01:10:05,436
[SPEAKER_00]: You have it because you need to eat.

959
01:10:06,096 --> 01:10:06,576
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

960
01:10:06,756 --> 01:10:09,777
[SPEAKER_00]: If it's really low food, just like... And if you're like, oh, should I, should I, should I?

961
01:10:10,318 --> 01:10:16,680
[SPEAKER_01]: Just re-establish the mindfulness into why you need to eat and keep that thought while you're eating.

962
01:10:17,825 --> 01:10:29,453
[SPEAKER_01]: For as long as that door is present, while you're eating, no matter to what degree it's present, sometimes more, sometimes less, if you're establishing it mindfully, as an anchor, you'll be eating for the right reasons, no matter what.

963
01:10:30,554 --> 01:10:45,725
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's, you know, I remember I met people, monks, who always, you know, a big dhāna, loads of food, like, I don't know, 50 dishes, and then, instead of taking responsibility for the fact that you have to eat,

964
01:10:46,837 --> 01:10:59,606
[SPEAKER_01]: And then eating what, you know, you find agreeable, not necessarily always what you really, really like, but say, you know, I don't like certain things, but I'll take them, because I learned that they are very nutritional, that they can keep me going further.

965
01:11:00,507 --> 01:11:01,508
[SPEAKER_01]: So I will have to eat less.

966
01:11:01,928 --> 01:11:02,228
[SPEAKER_01]: Great.

967
01:11:02,328 --> 01:11:03,589
[SPEAKER_01]: You go for that, even if you don't like.

968
01:11:03,949 --> 01:11:11,134
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes I find out that this really thing that I really happen to like, I really, I love the taste of that, it's also very, very good for you.

969
01:11:11,635 --> 01:11:12,215
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll take that.

970
01:11:12,736 --> 01:11:15,337
[SPEAKER_01]: Either way, I will not forget why I need to eat.

971
01:11:15,518 --> 01:11:15,778
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

972
01:11:16,463 --> 01:11:23,928
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, those monks would not necessarily think like... well, they would not descend to that level, so they would recognize the problem of preference.

973
01:11:24,808 --> 01:11:28,351
[SPEAKER_01]: That kind of preference is not a problem, but preference-inducing lust is a problem.

974
01:11:28,911 --> 01:11:32,573
[SPEAKER_01]: But instead of recognizing, taking up responsibility for it, they try to deny it.

975
01:11:33,014 --> 01:11:34,975
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they would either always take what they don't like,

976
01:11:36,041 --> 01:11:37,583
[SPEAKER_01]: I always take what I want less.

977
01:11:38,284 --> 01:11:45,111
[SPEAKER_01]: That means, okay, so you're basically attributing choice to the view of going after that which is less desirable.

978
01:11:45,432 --> 01:11:46,493
[SPEAKER_01]: I am not responsible.

979
01:11:47,174 --> 01:11:48,035
[SPEAKER_01]: There are three choices.

980
01:11:48,755 --> 01:11:50,097
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll go for the one I least want.

981
01:11:51,398 --> 01:11:53,481
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's already something you've chosen beforehand.

982
01:11:54,280 --> 01:11:55,341
[SPEAKER_01]: But now you're attributing it.

983
01:11:55,821 --> 01:12:01,765
[SPEAKER_01]: And then I even met some monks who were like saying, I will take only every third dish, whatever that dish might be.

984
01:12:02,506 --> 01:12:06,288
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, so now you're attributing responsibility to the chance.

985
01:12:07,449 --> 01:12:12,272
[SPEAKER_01]: See, all of that is irrelevant, actually, if they were to remain mindful as to why they're eating.

986
01:12:13,393 --> 01:12:19,938
[SPEAKER_01]: But clearly, the failure of putting on importance of how the dishes are chosen, means they're not mindful when they were eating.

987
01:12:20,793 --> 01:12:20,993
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

988
01:12:21,053 --> 01:12:23,594
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, hey, I didn't choose out of my preference.

989
01:12:23,654 --> 01:12:27,135
[SPEAKER_01]: I've chosen out of this every-third-dish algorithm that I wrote.

990
01:12:27,996 --> 01:12:30,516
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, I can forget about it, because now it's fine.

991
01:12:30,556 --> 01:12:31,737
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever I have in my bowl, it's fine.

992
01:12:31,897 --> 01:12:32,677
[SPEAKER_01]: None of it is fine.

993
01:12:33,137 --> 01:12:33,958
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you should start.

994
01:12:34,538 --> 01:12:37,619
[SPEAKER_01]: No food is fine to eat, good or bad.

995
01:12:39,720 --> 01:12:41,460
[SPEAKER_01]: You only have to eat because you want to survive.

996
01:12:42,521 --> 01:12:48,783
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you keep that, then you wouldn't care what food is in your bowl, whether it's tasty or not, because you realize none of it is fine.

997
01:12:50,105 --> 01:12:52,126
[SPEAKER_01]: But they all come from the point of view that food is fine.

998
01:12:52,727 --> 01:12:57,030
[SPEAKER_01]: If in some way there's a bigger problem than the other, then you try to avoid by choosing the opposite, da-da-da-da-da.

999
01:12:57,871 --> 01:13:03,975
[SPEAKER_01]: Point being, none of that would actually be a problem for them, if they were to remain mindful while they're eating, as to why.

1000
01:13:05,136 --> 01:13:07,337
[SPEAKER_01]: While they're eating, as to why they're eating.

1001
01:13:08,158 --> 01:13:09,239
[SPEAKER_01]: Hungry, full stomach.

1002
01:13:09,379 --> 01:13:10,880
[SPEAKER_01]: Hungry, full stomach.

1003
01:13:10,960 --> 01:13:11,781
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, this is inevitable.

1004
01:13:11,801 --> 01:13:14,983
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, it's impossible to eat without giving in to the

1005
01:13:16,714 --> 01:13:20,977
[SPEAKER_01]: There's a sense domain of taste to the animal that pertains to that domain, to that pool.

1006
01:13:21,838 --> 01:13:23,779
[SPEAKER_01]: But what I can do is keep it in check.

1007
01:13:24,179 --> 01:13:28,302
[SPEAKER_01]: I let it eat, because it needs to eat, but I'll keep it in check as to...

1008
01:13:28,883 --> 01:13:36,348
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll ground it, I'll train it to the reason why I'm eating, which is to sustain this body no more.

1009
01:13:37,729 --> 01:13:44,674
[SPEAKER_01]: So, on some days, there will be food that that animal likes, that the sense of taste

1010
01:13:46,382 --> 01:13:47,282
[SPEAKER_01]: Finds it agreeable.

1011
01:13:47,702 --> 01:13:48,703
[SPEAKER_01]: Defines it disagreeable.

1012
01:13:49,143 --> 01:13:53,904
[SPEAKER_01]: But you won't be bothered by going through all this effort of always finding a disagreeable taste.

1013
01:13:54,284 --> 01:13:57,445
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you realize, agreeable or disagreeable, both are in the same domain.

1014
01:13:58,105 --> 01:13:58,925
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's not the problem.

1015
01:13:59,365 --> 01:14:00,926
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is that I was affected by it.

1016
01:14:02,906 --> 01:14:04,966
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can be equally affected by disagreeable.

1017
01:14:06,087 --> 01:14:14,069
[SPEAKER_01]: Because sometimes, if you don't... Like, if you always go around choosing the disagreeable taste, sometimes you're presented by tastes and none of them is disagreeable.

1018
01:14:14,669 --> 01:14:15,569
[SPEAKER_01]: What are you going to choose then?

1019
01:14:17,113 --> 01:14:25,420
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you won't be able to not be affected by agreeable taste, because you were running away from it into disagreeable, which was also on the level of taste.

1020
01:14:26,021 --> 01:14:31,726
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't care about agreeable taste or disagreeable taste, you care about the nature of taste affecting you.

1021
01:14:31,746 --> 01:14:43,797
[SPEAKER_01]: And that can be undone, or that can be accomplished, not being affected by that, can be accomplished simply by remaining mindful as to why do you need... why you need to give in to the taste in the first place, be it agreeable, disagreeable or mutual.

1022
01:14:45,402 --> 01:14:49,424
[SPEAKER_01]: And when you keep mind... when you develop enough mindfulness in regard to that, then you wouldn't care what you're eating.

1023
01:14:50,365 --> 01:14:51,305
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't care what you're choosing.

1024
01:14:51,325 --> 01:14:52,286
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't care how you're choosing.

1025
01:14:52,726 --> 01:14:55,647
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't care if somebody else puts the food in your bowl, or if you go and put the food in your bowl.

1026
01:14:56,028 --> 01:14:58,209
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't care if you're just going to choose the agreeable stuff.

1027
01:14:58,969 --> 01:15:02,731
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're not affected by agreeable, none more than you're affected by disagreeable.

1028
01:15:02,851 --> 01:15:03,171
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not.

1029
01:15:03,231 --> 01:15:03,912
[SPEAKER_01]: You're beyond both.

1030
01:15:06,153 --> 01:15:07,374
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you won't be overeating.

1031
01:15:08,334 --> 01:15:10,615
[SPEAKER_01]: Out of indulgence, you won't be... Under-eating.

1032
01:15:10,655 --> 01:15:11,155
[SPEAKER_00]: Under-eating

